ave the RTWR","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T12:20:57-07:00","id":1524144,"title":"","content":"I search in Storyteller Vault but i not find scenarios for VR2th","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T15:53:11-07:00","id":1524157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524137-scenarios-for-vampire-the-requiem-2th#post1524137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings storytellers and players, I'm looking for inspiration in Vampire The Requiem 2th scenarios but I can't find examples of ready-made scenarios with plots, pdms and setting.<br /> Can you help me with links or sources of ideas and ready-made scenarios for Vampire The Requiem 2th?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, no idea - all materials related to adventures or city books i do have are from 1e.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524137-scenarios-for-vampire-the-requiem-2th#post1524137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have New Orleans but the math of the characters I don't like,</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, what exactly you disliked - i'm not quite sure i got what you meant.<br /> As an aside, the Danse de La Mort intro chronicle for Requiem can add some color and twists to the city's cast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524137-scenarios-for-vampire-the-requiem-2th#post1524137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago is interesting but I think it serves better as a crossover than a scenario focused on vampires.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one can always say &quot;gank fluff as writen and let me pilfer and adapt&quot; - no qualms about using Cihuateteo from Night Horrors: Wicked Dead or Sons of Phobos from Blood Sorcery in place of the canon Awakened, ghoul families with an affinity for Protean and weird religious practices in place of Uratha or whatever might strike one's fancy.<br /> <br /> I remember once using the 1e corebook's New Orleans and its focus on Catholic Lancea Sanctum x Crone <i>voudounsaints</i> as basis for a version of the city of Salvador influenced by <i>O Pagador de Promessas</i> and some works from Jorge Amado for a short &quot;test game&quot; of sorts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}